DTLS / ICE diagnostics for libpeer (extern/libpeer).

extern/libpeer is a git SUBMODULE, so its sources must not be edited in
place: the next `git submodule update` would throw the changes away.  This
patch is applied to the checked out tree by
tools/apply-libpeer-switch-patches.sh, right before libpeer is built (it is
the fourth patch of that series, after 0001-switch-webrtc-fixes,
0002-no-stdout-log and 0003-h265-depacketizer).

Why
---
The engine could not tell WHY a DTLS handshake failed:

  * peer_connection_loop() kept the handshake's return code in a LOCAL
    variable (`dtls_ret`).  It died with the stack frame, and the only
    trace was a LOGE() that 0022 had turned off.
  * `lastDtlsWrite` (the stat the engine exposed) comes from
    dtls_srtp_write() -- that is the SCTP payload write, NOT the handshake.
  * libpeer's own diagnostic channel (peer_connection_diag_log(): dtls_start,
    dtls_pending ret=<code>, ice_pair[..], ice_consent) needs BOTH a
    callback and the "enabled" flag.  The engine set neither, so the whole
    DTLS/ICE story was invisible.

What it adds
------------
1. src/dtls_srtp.h / src/dtls_srtp.c -- the handshake verdict survives:

     last_mbedtls_ret      raw return code of the last
                           mbedtls_ssl_handshake() step
     fingerprint_check     0 unknown / 1 match / -1 mismatch /
                           -2 no peer certificate
     handshake_active      1 while mbedtls_ssl_handshake() runs
     last_write_is_handshake
                           1 when the last DTLS record that went out was a
                           handshake record (0 = application data)
     remote_fingerprint_alg
                           the algorithm of the fingerprint the peer
                           announced

   The "fingerprint mismatch" log line now prints the algorithm, the length
   and the first 8 characters instead of the two full fingerprints: a
   fingerprint is a public negotiated value, but there is no reason to put
   the whole thing into a log file.

2. src/peer_connection.h / src/peer_connection.c -- a snapshot API:

     int peer_connection_get_diagnostics(PeerConnection* pc,
                                         PeerConnectionDiagnostics* out);

   It reports the DTLS state / role / handshake verdict / fingerprint
   summaries / handshake timing, and the ICE consent counters, the candidate
   pairs (local + remote address, type, state, conncheck count) and the
   local candidates.

   The fingerprints are reduced to algorithm + length + the first 8
   characters INSIDE libpeer, so the full value never crosses the library
   boundary.

3. The offer is read a second time (diagnostics only): the a=setup: value
   and the fingerprint the offer really carries.  The comparison in
   peer_connection_set_remote_description() is left EXACTLY as it was --
   this patch changes no behaviour of the handshake, it only makes the
   outcome observable.

★ No DTLS key material is logged or exported.  The printf block that dumped
  the key material was deleted by 0022; nothing here touches it.
